- Subject identity, face, clothing, weapons, limb count, structure, or art style changes without cause;
- A similar appearance is written directly as a confirmed character, or a real person's identity is guessed from a face alone;
- A confirmed character uses behavior clearly conflicting with their personality, combat habits, ability system, or version, and the user did not request a rewrite;
- A single-subject set of images has an evenly matched new protagonist added without authorization;
- Adjacent shots' positions, facings, speeds, or weapon states suddenly reset;
- During the climax, camera, subjects, targets, media, debris, and fabric all lose motion simultaneously;
- Camera settle, subject braking, and environmental decay are conflated into a single stop command;
- Effects have no source, or environmental destruction runs opposite to the action's force direction;
- Important attacks end at contact or eruption with no readable result;
- The four shots' timecodes are wrong, shots are missing, or any sound section is missing;
