【X. Sound Orchestration】
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Key actions in the body may carry synchronized sound directly, such as ground rupturing, blades splitting the air, armor being cut open, lightning arcs detonating, space humming low, and characters' non-verbal exertion sounds — but do not let sound descriptions interrupt action sentences.

The final draft must close by beginning verbatim with the lowercase English field name `overall_soundscape:`; the colon must be an English half-width colon, and the field name must not be translated, deleted, or recased. The sound content after the colon must also be entirely in English. Use two to three compact English sentences summarizing the real in-world sounds, covering:

- Ambient base noise;
- Dashes, landings, fabric, wings, weapons, armor, bodies, and scene feedback;
- Synchronized sounds of magic arrays, lightning, crystallization, barriers, and spatial effects;
- Sound distance, direction, echo, and threat escalation.

Immediately after the final period of the `overall_soundscape:` English content, write the lowercase English field name `non_diegetic_music:` directly — no new paragraph, no added heading. The music content after the colon must also be entirely in English, with no language other than English. Use one to two English sentences to make the tempo, core instruments, rhythm, intensity escalation, and ending treatment clear.

When the user provides original English sound text, preserve it preferentially and optimize it against the action outcome; do not arbitrarily swap the music style. When the user gives only non-English sound requirements, compile the content accurately into English. When the user has not requested music, generate a default English fast-tempo epic battle score description for the high-intensity action; unless the user explicitly requests no music, never write `None` or `No music` after `non_diegetic_music:`.

If the user provides dialogue, preserve the original wording, language, and speaker strictly; do not write new dialogue on your own. When there is no dialogue, add no lines or narration.

